# Most build output regenerates from model/*.py and stays out of here.
# THE EXCEPTIONS, committed deliberately: the .blend, the STLs and
# report.json. They are still generated files, so they will show up as
# unreviewable binary diffs on every run - that cost is accepted so the repo
# carries something you can open without Blender installed and a build run,
# and so a fresh clone is a complete board rather than a recipe for one.
# REGENERATE, do not hand-edit: any change made inside Blender is lost the
# next time blender_board.py runs.

# Blender's rolling auto-backup. Pure noise, never useful in a diff.
model/efoil_v2.blend1
*.blend1

# viewport renders and diagrams - 173 MB of build output, still excluded
renders/

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party product imagery: Lift, Fliteboard and Waydoo marketing renders
# and photos, collected as shape reference while drawing the hull. Fine to
# keep on disk for our own reference, NOT ours to redistribute - and this repo
# is one visibility flip away from being public. Kept out deliberately.
reference/

# report.json IS now committed - see the note at the top. One caveat that
# comes with it: bom.py refuses to run if report.json is OLDER than
# blender_board.py, but a fresh clone gives every file the same checkout
# time, so that guard cannot see staleness that was committed IN. It catches
# drift you create locally, not drift someone else pushed. Re-run the model
# after pulling if the numbers matter.
